<title>THAILAND: Thai bourse lifts suspension on Union Bank.</title>
<headline>Thai bourse lifts suspension on Union Bank.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand on Tuesday lifted its trading suspension on the shares of the Union Bank of Bangkok Plc following disclosure of the bank's decision to pay no dividend for 1996.</p>
<p>The shares were suspended on April 4 after the bank failed to inform the exchange of resolutions made at its recent shareholders meeting.</p>
</text>
